{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02394",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.71,
      "end_seconds": 3.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.63,
      "end_seconds": 12.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.99,
      "end_seconds": 25.47,
      "duration_seconds": 11.48,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come. It's itchy spots all over, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.31,
      "end_seconds": 29.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.51,
      "end_seconds": 35.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Okay, so I'd say about a month, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 37.06,
      "end_seconds": 42.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Uh, hm, I'd say more like about two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.11,
      "end_seconds": 47.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.47,
      "end_seconds": 50.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "That sounds about right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.94,
      "end_seconds": 55.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.28,
      "end_seconds": 58.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.46,
      "end_seconds": 66.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 66.43,
      "end_seconds": 71.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.69,
      "end_seconds": 80.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I was getting to that! Oh, and a mild temperature."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.0,
      "end_seconds": 88.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "Have you had itchy spots all over before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.53,
      "end_seconds": 95.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "I, I had a similar thing about six months ago. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.63,
      "end_seconds": 116.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "And what about pregnancy or being immunosuppressed?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.44,
      "end_seconds": 126.88,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "No, no pregnancy, no being immunosuppressed. I was feeling achy at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.77,
      "end_seconds": 132.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Have you noticed stiff neck or breathlessness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.42,
      "end_seconds": 138.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Let me think, I haven't had stiff neck or breathlessness, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.27,
      "end_seconds": 144.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Alright, anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.99,
      "end_seconds": 147.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.37,
      "end_seconds": 150.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 152.52,
      "end_seconds": 157.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "She takes spironolactone, 25 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.24,
      "end_seconds": 162.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Before this I was on ramipril; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.19,
      "end_seconds": 165.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.11,
      "end_seconds": 179.24,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "I've had heart failure, yes. Mm, um, I have high blood pressure, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.94,
      "end_seconds": 182.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.74,
      "end_seconds": 190.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.8,
      "end_seconds": 192.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Alright, any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.67,
      "end_seconds": 197.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.06,
      "end_seconds": 200.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "How active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.25,
      "end_seconds": 205.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.62,
      "end_seconds": 227.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.94,
      "end_seconds": 246.71,
      "duration_seconds": 13.77,
      "text": "Yes, amoxicillin. I've no idea what the reaction was, only that I'm not supposed to have it. Wheat. I come out in... well, bloating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.46,
      "end_seconds": 249.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.58,
      "end_seconds": 258.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "I, I had my appendix taken out when I was in my twenties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.01,
      "end_seconds": 264.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.69,
      "end_seconds": 274.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.57,
      "end_seconds": 292.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 117 over 78, temperature 36.6. And respiratory rate 15, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, heart rate 86."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.78,
      "end_seconds": 297.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.88,
      "end_seconds": 301.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.2,
      "end_seconds": 322.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "There are crops of blisters and scabs in different stages on the trunk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.01,
      "end_seconds": 325.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.57,
      "end_seconds": 357.69,
      "duration_seconds": 28.12,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Putting it all together, I'd lean towards chickenpox. We shouldn't forget shingles. What I'm giving you is aciclovir, 800 milligrams, five times a day, seven days. That should help with adult chickenpox. Stay at home until all the spots have crusted and stay away from pregnant women. If you smoke, this is a good moment to think about stopping, and we can help you with that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.35,
      "end_seconds": 372.58,
      "duration_seconds": 13.23,
      "text": "If you become breathless or have chest pain, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. I'd like to see you again if you become breathless."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 374.41,
      "end_seconds": 378.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I can put that appointment in for you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.19,
      "end_seconds": 382.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Okay, does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.81,
      "end_seconds": 387.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Thank you, you know, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}